  on a grid and just print it out  the downside is you have to do a  dimensionality reduction because you  just can display it on 2d or 3d  but it's also a good a good method if  you're working on this  i can only recommend you i'm taking this  this example out  you can see here we are in layer 11 and  and this is the interactive website  where you can  have a look at how  the bird model in this case  answers faq questions and you can see  each step from layer 1 to layer 12 and  how the model moves around the words and  takes them into  yeah  into  correlation so it's very cool and you  can find the link in my presentation i  will upload it  later on  so these were  like my ideas for  tackling explainability for  for nlp models um i've just summarized  it to you so you can find it later in  the slides  what are now the main difficulties um  i have spoken of so  first you have the high number of  dimensions as you might already know you  have a high variability in models so you  could have like a bag of words  representation of your words you could  have embeddings  that you  want to feed into your model so this  variability leads to yeah difficulties  because i cannot say this is the one  solution that you should use here  um then the next problem is  a set of tokens is not equal to  variables so if you have the same token  in different positions in the text it  has a different meaning because of the  context because of the  yeah the contents of the whole text and  in this case you have to treat text more  like image data than numerical data and  this is something you have to remember  then it's very difficult to make the  transfer from local to global some  models can do this some other models  can't and it's important to keep that in  mind  yeah it's also difficult to show  something graphically because even if  you have word embeddings you have to  reduce the  dimensionality in order to show them you  don't want to print out all of your word  vectors into a dicti